PVC not available

PVC = PersistentVolumeClaim
A Pod may need storage:
Pod
 ↓
PVC
 ↓
Storage

If the Pod asks for a PVC but that PVC is not available, the Pod may remain Pending.
Example Deployment:

volumes:
  - name: app-storage
    persistentVolumeClaim:
      claimName: my-pvc

But:  kubectl get pvc
shows:
NAME      STATUS     VOLUME
my-pvc    Pending

Then the Pod cannot get its required storage.

Check:
kubectl get pvc
kubectl describe pvc my-pvc
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>

You may see an event such as:
FailedScheduling
pod has unbound immediate PersistentVolumeClaims

Simple meaning
Pod says: "I need this storage."
PVC says: "I haven't got storage yet."
Therefore Pod waits → Pending.
