So if readiness fails, Kubernetes normally does NOT restart the container. The Pod is removed from the Service's ready endpoints.

Liveness fails
    ↓
Container restarted

Readiness fails
    ↓
No traffic sent to Pod
    ↓
Container keeps running




not have / health means not have the folder
