----------------
Memory leak means the application keeps using memory but doesn't release memory that it no longer needs.

Example:
Application starts
    ↓
Uses 200 MB
    ↓
Handles requests
    ↓
Uses 300 MB
    ↓
More requests
    ↓
Uses 400 MB
    ↓
More requests
    ↓
Uses 500 MB
    ↓
Uses 600 MB
    ↓
Memory limit = 512 MB
    ↓
OOMKilled ❌

So even though the application is not intentionally asking for more and more memory, some unused objects/data remain in memory.

Interview definition:
A memory leak is when an application continuously consumes memory without properly releasing unused memory,
causing memory usage to grow over time and potentially resulting in OOMKilled.



1. Large requests

This means the application receives a large amount of data in one request.
Example:

Normal request → 10 MB
Large request  → 2 GB

The application may need much more memory to process the large request.

Example:

Memory limit = 512Mi
       ↓
Large request needs 700Mi
       ↓
Memory > 512Mi
       ↓
OOMKilled



2. JVM heap configuration

This applies to Java applications.
The JVM uses part of the container's memory for the Java heap.

Example:
Container memory limit = 512Mi
JVM heap = 450Mi

The application also needs memory for things outside the heap—such as threads, native memory, and class metadata.

So the total can exceed the container limit:

JVM heap        = 450Mi
Other memory    = 150Mi
-----------------------
Total           = 600Mi
Container limit = 512Mi

Result:
600Mi > 512Mi
     ↓
OOMKilled

Java heap means the part of memory where a Java application stores objects and data created while the application is running.
For example:

Java application
      ↓
Creates objects/data
      ↓
Java Heap
      ↓
Memory used

3. Application memory usage
This simply means how much memory the application is actually using.
Check it with:  kubectl top pod <pod-name>

Example:
NAME       CPU    MEMORY
myapp      200m   600Mi

If your Deployment has:
limits:
  memory: "512Mi"

but the application uses: 600Mi
then it can be:
600Mi > 512Mi
      ↓
OOMKilled
